    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d195">

                <pb facs="0365" n="265" sameAs="frus:frus1884/pg265"/>

                <head>No. 195.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Frelinghuysen to Mr.
                    Daggett.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1883-12-13"><hi rendition="#italic">December</hi> 13,
                        1883</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 43.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Adverting to the instruction sent to you
                    upon the 15th ultimo, No. 38, I have now to transmit, for your information, the
                    inclosed copies of correspondence between the Hawaiian minister here and myself,
                    touching the complaint of the Pacific Mail Steamship Company against the
                    Government of Hawaii.</p>
                <p>The Department’s reply to Mr. Carter is sufficiently explicit to render any
                    special instructions to you in the premises unnecessary.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>FRED’K T. FRELINGHUYSEN.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
